<title>USA: Mark IV to restructure, sees $1.04/shr chg.</title>
<headline>Mark IV to restructure, sees $1.04/shr chg.</headline>
<dateline>AMHERST, N.Y. 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mark IV Industries Inc said Wednesday it will undertake a major restructuring, eliminating 1,000 jobs and resulting in an after-tax charge of about $66 million, or $1.04 per fully diluted share.</p>
<p>Total charges amount to about $110 million before taxes, some $60 million of which will be non-cash to account for the write-down of long-term assets, Mark IV said.</p>
<p>The move will be recorded in the third quarter, sending the period into the loss column.</p>
<p>Mark IV said it expects to meet analysts' expectations of $1.65-$1.70 per share for fiscal year 1996 before the charges.  </p>
<p>Mark IV said it expects to realize pre-tax savings of between $40 and $45 million per year, or $0.38 to $0.43 per share after taxes.</p>
</text>
